    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d423-a3">

                <pb facs="0443" n="423" sameAs="frus:frus1864p3/pg423"/>


                <head>Mr. Burlingame to Prince
                        Kung</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United
                            States,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-12-23"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 23, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge your
                    despatch relating to General Burgevine, and beg to inform you that I have
                    received information from the United States consul at Shanghai that he arrested
                    him last month and held him <pb facs="0444" n="424" xml:id="pg424"/> for trial,
                    and did not allow him to go at liberty in Shanghai. But because of his wound
                    received at Sung-kiang in fighting the rebels, which still was not yet fully
                    healed, he desired a short delay to effect a cure, when he would leave China and
                    return to America.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ANSON BURLINGAME.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Imperial Highness <hi rendition="#small-caps">Prince Kung.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
